1
00:01:36,953 --> 00:01:37,620
"DAIJIRO OHARA"

2
00:01:37,821 --> 00:01:38,688
Thank you.

3
00:01:43,026 --> 00:01:44,461
It's so cold, isn't it?

4
00:01:44,661 --> 00:01:47,530
Who wants to go out on patrol on a chilly day like this?

5
00:01:47,764 --> 00:01:50,133
Ryo-san, you always say things like that.

6
00:01:52,001 --> 00:01:54,170
Ryo-chan. There's a postcard for you.

7
00:01:54,637 --> 00:01:57,140
Probably just mail-order junk. Throw it away.

8
00:01:57,707 --> 00:01:59,409
It doesn't look like mail-order.

9
00:01:59,642 --> 00:02:01,711
Let's see... It's from...

10
00:02:01,945 --> 00:02:03,146
Yone Ryotsu.

11
00:02:03,646 --> 00:02:04,414
What?

12
00:02:05,315 --> 00:02:07,851
Ryo-san, isn't that your mom?

13
00:02:08,051 --> 00:02:08,985
Yeah, yeah.

14
00:02:10,987 --> 00:02:11,788
Oh!

15
00:02:15,225 --> 00:02:16,893
Ryo-chan! Why did you do that?

16
00:02:17,327 --> 00:02:19,496
Mail-order would have been less trouble.

17
00:02:19,696 --> 00:02:20,897
I'm going on patrol.

18
00:02:25,034 --> 00:02:25,668
Huh?

19
00:02:25,869 --> 00:02:26,603
Hmm?

20
00:02:28,438 --> 00:02:32,675
"Dear Kankichi, I am well.

21
00:02:32,876 --> 00:02:36,146
No matter how many postcards I send, you never write back.

22
00:02:36,346 --> 00:02:38,848
&lt;i&gt;They say that no news is good news,&lt;/i&gt;

23
00:02:39,048 --> 00:02:42,252
&lt;i&gt;but it pains me to have not&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;heard from you for so many years.&lt;/i&gt;

24
00:02:42,752 --> 00:02:47,457
&lt;i&gt;Your dad's not doing well after getting&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;a hernia at the end of last year.&lt;/i&gt;

25
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:50,827
&lt;i&gt;Some days he never even gets out of bed.&lt;/i&gt;

26
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:56,099
&lt;i&gt;Kankichi, please stop all this fuss&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and let us see your face just once more.&lt;/i&gt;

27
00:02:56,299 --> 00:02:59,435
&lt;i&gt;I'm sure it would make&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;your dad feel better too.&lt;/i&gt;

28
00:02:59,636 --> 00:03:02,038
&lt;i&gt;We're your family. Please come home.&lt;/i&gt;

29
00:03:02,238 --> 00:03:04,908
&lt;i&gt;Take care not to catch&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;a cold in this weather.&lt;/i&gt;

30
00:03:05,108 --> 00:03:06,276
&lt;i&gt;From Mom."&lt;/i&gt;

31
00:03:07,010 --> 00:03:07,777
Oh!

32
00:03:08,745 --> 00:03:09,946
Ryo-chan, wait!

33
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,281
What?

34
00:03:11,481 --> 00:03:13,616
Why don't you ever go see your parents?

35
00:03:14,017 --> 00:03:17,086
What's it to you? I hate tsukudani and being lectured!

36
00:03:17,287 --> 00:03:18,188
Goodbye!

37
00:03:18,388 --> 00:03:19,889
Oh, Ryo-chan!

38
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:25,461
Leave him be. He gets in a really bad mood whenever anyone talks about his family.

39
00:03:25,662 --> 00:03:30,099
Come to think of it, he never mentions his family, does he?

40
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,669
Some topics are off limits for some people.

41
00:03:32,902 --> 00:03:33,803
Chief!

42
00:03:36,206 --> 00:03:39,309
You said there's something Ryotsu doesn't want to tell us?

43
00:03:41,044 --> 00:03:43,479
I don't know the full story...

44
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:48,151
&lt;i&gt;He ran away from home at 18&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;after a huge fight with his father.&lt;/i&gt;

45
00:03:48,351 --> 00:03:50,153
&lt;i&gt;He hasn't been back since.&lt;/i&gt;

46
00:03:50,353 --> 00:03:54,123
&lt;i&gt;So the postcard was right?&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;He hasn't been back in years?&lt;/i&gt;

47
00:03:54,324 --> 00:03:58,795
&lt;i&gt;Yep. I told him to stop with these&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;silly grudges and just go see his parents.&lt;/i&gt;

48
00:03:58,995 --> 00:04:03,233
&lt;i&gt;I tried to convince him, saying there's&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;no place like home, but it was no use.&lt;/i&gt;

49
00:04:03,633 --> 00:04:07,270
&lt;i&gt;He said he'd need a sweet sister&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to go home to, which makes no sense.&lt;/i&gt;

50
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:10,540
&lt;i&gt;He did say he hates&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tsukudani and being lectured.&lt;/i&gt;

51
00:04:11,074 --> 00:04:12,809
&lt;i&gt;Every summer and every winter,&lt;/i&gt;

52
00:04:13,009 --> 00:04:16,279
&lt;i&gt;his parents send tsukudani&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;gift packages to the station.&lt;/i&gt;

53
00:04:16,946 --> 00:04:21,918
&lt;i&gt;There's always an accompanying letter&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;thanking us for looking after him.&lt;/i&gt;

54
00:04:22,118 --> 00:04:25,288
&lt;i&gt;Sounds like Ryo-chan has a lovely family.&lt;/i&gt;

55
00:04:25,722 --> 00:04:28,992
Hey, why don't we help Ryo-chan and his dad make up?

56
00:04:29,526 --> 00:04:31,160
Isn't that a great idea?

57
00:04:31,361 --> 00:04:32,128
Huh?

58
00:04:32,328 --> 00:04:33,363
Eh?

59
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:37,367
Then his mom won't have to write any more of these postcards either.

60
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:38,968
Just let it be.

61
00:04:39,168 --> 00:04:42,038
Getting involved will only bring you grief.

62
00:04:44,307 --> 00:04:46,743
Damn it, someone's talking about me.

63
00:04:47,277 --> 00:04:49,145
What are you doing?

64
00:04:49,345 --> 00:04:51,547
My back's feeling a little better today,

65
00:04:51,748 --> 00:04:54,484
so I thought I'd go and pray at Sensoji Temple.

66
00:04:54,684 --> 00:04:56,019
Hold it.

67
00:04:56,853 --> 00:04:59,155
You need a horse racing paper to pray?

68
00:04:59,756 --> 00:05:01,524
Oh, this is, um...

69
00:05:01,724 --> 00:05:03,660
All this sleep has dulled the mind.

70
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:06,195
It's called exercising your brain. See you!

71
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:08,064
Wait!

72
00:05:08,564 --> 00:05:13,236
Jeez, you only hurt your back in the first place by getting too excited after a win.

73
00:05:17,206 --> 00:05:17,840
Huh?

74
00:05:18,241 --> 00:05:21,577
Ryotsu, come here for a minute. We've got something to show you.

75
00:05:22,045 --> 00:05:23,413
Something to show me?

76
00:05:24,247 --> 00:05:26,416
So what? It's just a navigation system.

77
00:05:26,883 --> 00:05:29,986
It's not just any navigation system.

78
00:05:30,887 --> 00:05:33,590
It's a super system made by one of my companies.

79
00:05:35,558 --> 00:05:39,729
It has traffic information, and details on every dwelling in Japan.

80
00:05:39,929 --> 00:05:44,000
It can even point out popular date spots and hidden-gem restaurants.

81
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,270
Wow, I didn't know you could get so detailed.

82
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:51,174
Let's set a destination and start the navigation.

83
00:05:51,374 --> 00:05:53,009
Anywhere you'd like to go?

84
00:05:53,209 --> 00:05:56,713
In all my time since coming to Tokyo, I've never been to Asakusa.

85
00:05:56,913 --> 00:05:58,247
Can we go there?

86
00:05:58,448 --> 00:06:00,450
No, not there. Choose somewhere else.

87
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:01,284
Why?

88
00:06:01,818 --> 00:06:04,787
No reason. I'm just saying no to Asakusa.

89
00:06:05,254 --> 00:06:08,958
Well, I guess it does give off kind of a drab image.

90
00:06:09,392 --> 00:06:12,462
He's right. There's nothing to do in Asakusa.

91
00:06:12,662 --> 00:06:15,231
It's full of old people, and it's tacky.

92
00:06:16,432 --> 00:06:19,469
True, true. I doubt there's anything worth seeing there.

93
00:06:19,669 --> 00:06:21,671
Let's go to Roppongi or Shibuya instead.

94
00:06:22,839 --> 00:06:25,274
Are you kidding? You think Asakusa is tacky?

95
00:06:25,475 --> 00:06:26,976
Quit joking around!

96
00:06:27,210 --> 00:06:28,144
What's the matter?

97
00:06:28,444 --> 00:06:31,614
Asakusa has been Japan's cultural center since the 1600s!

98
00:06:31,814 --> 00:06:35,752
Compared to Asakusa, Roppongi and Shibuya are just little pups!

99
00:06:35,952 --> 00:06:37,253
But you just said...

100
00:06:37,453 --> 00:06:40,757
Not another word! "Nothing worth seeing"? We'll see about that!

101
00:06:40,957 --> 00:06:44,327
I'll show you what a gem Asakusa is.

102
00:06:51,634 --> 00:06:54,303
&lt;i&gt;Good morning! Let's start the route guide.&lt;/i&gt;

103
00:06:54,504 --> 00:06:55,605
I know that voice!

104
00:06:55,805 --> 00:06:58,841
Isn't that Maya Katsuragi, the hit anime voice actress?

105
00:06:59,075 --> 00:07:01,678
&lt;i&gt;Ryo-chan, come with me to Asakusa!&lt;/i&gt;

106
00:07:01,878 --> 00:07:03,813
Sure thing, babe!

107
00:07:04,147 --> 00:07:06,315
He's talking to the navigation?

108
00:07:07,483 --> 00:07:11,721
You tell it your name and it guides you as if it's talking to you directly.

109
00:07:11,954 --> 00:07:15,958
This is the voice actress version, but there are lots of other versions too.

110
00:07:17,794 --> 00:07:21,731
&lt;i&gt;Mmm... Don't be in such a rush.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Let's take our time...&lt;/i&gt;

111
00:07:21,964 --> 00:07:23,733
What's this version?

112
00:07:23,966 --> 00:07:26,035
Nakagawa, I like this one.

113
00:07:26,269 --> 00:07:27,837
It's the porn star version.

114
00:07:28,037 --> 00:07:30,039
No! Change it to something else!

115
00:07:32,508 --> 00:07:35,211
Uh-oh, I was meant to turn left at the intersection.

116
00:07:35,445 --> 00:07:37,513
&lt;i&gt;Why didn't ya turn left, punk?&lt;/i&gt;

117
00:07:37,714 --> 00:07:38,848
&lt;i&gt;You bozo! Jackass!&lt;/i&gt;

118
00:07:39,048 --> 00:07:40,716
Hey, listen here, navigator!

119
00:07:40,917 --> 00:07:44,821
Ryo-chan, calm down. Punching it won't help.

120
00:07:45,021 --> 00:07:48,991
I think that's a no on the yakuza version for Ryotsu.

121
00:08:06,342 --> 00:08:09,579
Wow, there are so many tourists.

122
00:08:10,079 --> 00:08:12,048
Look at the huge paper lantern.

123
00:08:12,748 --> 00:08:14,550
Ryo-chan, what is this?

124
00:08:14,751 --> 00:08:17,920
You don't even know about Kaminarimon Gate? Good grief!

125
00:08:18,221 --> 00:08:21,491
That statue looks pretty scary. What is it?

126
00:08:21,691 --> 00:08:25,628
That's the god of thunder. And that one's the god of wind.

127
00:08:26,395 --> 00:08:29,432
And Nakamise Shopping Street leads to Sensoji Temple.

128
00:08:29,866 --> 00:08:33,102
It's only a weekday morning, but it's still pretty busy.

129
00:08:33,336 --> 00:08:35,438
Should have seen it back in the day.

130
00:08:49,552 --> 00:08:52,121
Freshly made food is the best.

131
00:08:56,826 --> 00:08:58,961
-Come on, Ryo-chan! -Ryotsu!

132
00:08:59,195 --> 00:09:00,763
I want one of these too.

133
00:09:01,063 --> 00:09:02,565
These! Let's have these.

134
00:09:02,765 --> 00:09:04,300
Jeez, Ryo-chan!

135
00:09:05,401 --> 00:09:06,669
It's Kan-chan!

136
00:09:06,969 --> 00:09:08,371
How are you, ma'am?

137
00:09:08,571 --> 00:09:09,839
It's been so long.

138
00:09:10,072 --> 00:09:12,208
Hey, Kan-chan's back!

139
00:09:12,408 --> 00:09:14,644
Oh, Kankichi! Long time no see!

140
00:09:14,844 --> 00:09:15,912
Hey, it's you.

141
00:09:16,112 --> 00:09:19,815
Still on the drink and making the wife cry, I bet!

142
00:09:20,016 --> 00:09:22,652
How the heck did you become a cop!

143
00:09:22,852 --> 00:09:26,789
I so wanted to see the shop go under in three days under your name!

144
00:09:26,989 --> 00:09:27,924
Oh you!

145
00:09:29,225 --> 00:09:30,927
You never hold back, do you?

146
00:09:31,394 --> 00:09:34,697
It's been years, but Ryo-chan's still as popular as ever.

147
00:09:34,931 --> 00:09:38,100
This area is like his backyard, isn't it?

148
00:09:59,255 --> 00:10:02,692
Well then, shall we go to the Original Disneyland next?

149
00:10:03,125 --> 00:10:04,961
Original Disneyland?

150
00:10:19,642 --> 00:10:22,712
The roller coasters here are real thrill rides.

151
00:10:22,912 --> 00:10:25,848
You'll feel like you're about to crash into a house.

152
00:10:26,482 --> 00:10:30,052
Isn't your parents' house nearby? I'd like to go visit.

153
00:10:30,553 --> 00:10:31,187
Huh?

154
00:10:31,387 --> 00:10:35,324
Are you kidding me? We're on duty! Let's get back to work.

155
00:10:35,524 --> 00:10:39,695
I didn't know the words "on duty" were in your dictionary.

156
00:10:39,895 --> 00:10:43,733
Quiet! I haven't been home in years. Couldn't even tell you where it was.

157
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:46,302
That's okay. We've got the navigation system.

158
00:10:46,535 --> 00:10:47,303
What?

159
00:10:47,503 --> 00:10:49,305
We came all this way, after all.

160
00:10:49,505 --> 00:10:52,575
It'd be like coming to Asakusa and missing Sensoji Temple.

161
00:10:52,775 --> 00:10:56,245
That's what this was all about? You set me up! Hey, let go of me!

162
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:03,252
So that's your parents' house?

163
00:11:03,486 --> 00:11:05,888
Great. You've seen it. Can we go now?

164
00:11:06,088 --> 00:11:09,558
Seriously? We didn't come all this way to not even say hello.

165
00:11:09,759 --> 00:11:12,061
Hey, isn't that your mother?

166
00:11:12,795 --> 00:11:18,601
"GENERAL STORE"

167
00:11:18,968 --> 00:11:20,036
Come on, Ryotsu.

168
00:11:20,236 --> 00:11:22,505
No, I swore I'd never come back

169
00:11:22,705 --> 00:11:26,609
after that fight I had with my old man about taking over the shop.

170
00:11:26,809 --> 00:11:31,147
But hasn't your dad injured his back? You should go and see him.

171
00:11:31,681 --> 00:11:34,951
I cut off all ties with him. I can't go back now!

172
00:11:38,587 --> 00:11:39,956
I'll walk home.

173
00:11:40,690 --> 00:11:42,825
Ryo-chan! You've come all this way!

174
00:11:43,159 --> 00:11:46,829
Ryotsu, why not at least stay for dinner? I'll treat you.

175
00:11:47,396 --> 00:11:50,833
Oh, you will? If you're buying, then that's a different story.

176
00:11:51,067 --> 00:11:53,469
"EEL"

177
00:12:00,009 --> 00:12:01,944
Ooh, it's delicious.

178
00:12:02,178 --> 00:12:03,979
It's d"eel"-icious!

179
00:12:04,313 --> 00:12:08,117
Not only does it taste great, but the price is right too.

180
00:12:08,317 --> 00:12:12,154
The same taste and portion size would cost double back in Ginza.

181
00:12:12,388 --> 00:12:14,457
Well, Reiko? How's Asakusa now?

182
00:12:14,657 --> 00:12:16,759
Yes, you've converted me.

183
00:12:18,094 --> 00:12:20,963
That's right. Asakusa is number one!

184
00:12:21,163 --> 00:12:24,133
Asakusa Number One? Are you crazy?

185
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:26,035
Not on your life!

186
00:12:26,769 --> 00:12:30,606
Hell would sooner freeze over than see that sad old number as the winner.

187
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:34,176
Sure, it's the favorite, but nothing beats Roppongi.

188
00:12:34,777 --> 00:12:36,445
Roppongi?

189
00:12:36,645 --> 00:12:37,613
-Ryo-chan! -Ryotsu!

190
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:40,616
Hey! You disrespecting Asakusa?

191
00:12:40,816 --> 00:12:43,519
Listen, you old fart. You better watch your mouth.

192
00:12:43,753 --> 00:12:46,956
The gods may forgive you, but to me, that is a mortal sin!

193
00:12:47,156 --> 00:12:50,860
Who the hell are you to lay question on my bets?

194
00:13:10,146 --> 00:13:11,881
You...!

195
00:13:17,453 --> 00:13:18,487
-Huh? -Hmm?

196
00:13:19,221 --> 00:13:21,056
Ryotsu-san, I'm pretty sure...

197
00:13:21,257 --> 00:13:23,192
Shh... Shut up!

198
00:13:25,861 --> 00:13:28,397
What's going on? Do you know that man?

199
00:13:28,864 --> 00:13:31,467
Uh, well, I don't not know him...

200
00:13:31,901 --> 00:13:34,537
That other man called him Ryotsu-san.

201
00:13:34,737 --> 00:13:38,474
Yeah, there are a few around here. Don't worry about it.

202
00:13:38,674 --> 00:13:40,076
Is he perhaps your father?

203
00:13:40,276 --> 00:13:41,243
No!

204
00:13:41,477 --> 00:13:42,745
Then who is he?

205
00:13:43,579 --> 00:13:46,849
Well, he's married to...

206
00:13:47,049 --> 00:13:50,052
the woman who gave birth to me... a few decades ago.

207
00:13:50,286 --> 00:13:52,555
So he is your father!

208
00:13:53,022 --> 00:13:56,759
Well, I guess you could call it that, in general terms...

209
00:13:57,259 --> 00:13:58,527
Kei-chan, we did it!

210
00:13:58,727 --> 00:13:59,428
Yeah!

211
00:13:59,662 --> 00:14:01,564
Okay, Ryo-chan! Let's say hello.

212
00:14:01,764 --> 00:14:04,767
Shh! Not now. Later, later.

213
00:14:05,201 --> 00:14:06,769
There's no turning back now.

214
00:14:07,369 --> 00:14:08,871
That's right, Ryotsu!

215
00:14:10,039 --> 00:14:11,107
Come on!

216
00:14:11,307 --> 00:14:13,142
-Big fuss over there. -Ryo-chan!

217
00:14:13,375 --> 00:14:15,111
-Let's go! -No way! Stop that!

218
00:14:15,311 --> 00:14:16,445
Come on, Ryotsu.

219
00:14:16,946 --> 00:14:19,381
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

220
00:14:19,582 --> 00:14:21,217
My name is Keiichi Nakagawa.

221
00:14:21,417 --> 00:14:23,452
I am very much indebted to this guy.

222
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:27,223
I'm Reiko Akimoto. Nice to meet you.

223
00:14:27,423 --> 00:14:29,592
Oh, hello there.

224
00:14:29,959 --> 00:14:31,260
Ouch, that's hot!

225
00:14:31,861 --> 00:14:33,295
Are you okay?

226
00:14:33,529 --> 00:14:35,231
Yeah, it's nothing.

227
00:14:36,565 --> 00:14:40,703
Go on then. He's your father. At least say hello.

228
00:14:41,704 --> 00:14:42,538
Ryo-chan!

229
00:14:42,738 --> 00:14:43,772
Ryotsu!

230
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:45,174
Fine.

231
00:14:46,408 --> 00:14:48,277
H-Hello.

232
00:14:48,477 --> 00:14:51,714
I'm your son, Kankichi Ryotsu. Do you remember me?

233
00:14:52,815 --> 00:14:54,617
Oh, it's you?

234
00:14:54,817 --> 00:14:57,453
I thought I recognized your face from somewhere...

235
00:14:59,622 --> 00:15:01,790
That's a barefaced lie.

236
00:15:02,258 --> 00:15:03,959
Are they really father and son?

237
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:06,462
Yes, my confidence is fading.

238
00:15:06,896 --> 00:15:09,165
I won't interrupt your family reunion.

239
00:15:09,565 --> 00:15:10,499
Eh?

240
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,736
Ryotsu-san, I'll see you around.

241
00:15:13,936 --> 00:15:16,305
Wait! I still wanna make more bets!

242
00:15:16,672 --> 00:15:19,975
For the main race, a wheel bet on Makibao is a sure thing!

243
00:15:20,175 --> 00:15:21,977
Yes, yes. Enjoy yourself.

244
00:15:23,445 --> 00:15:25,447
Thank you.

245
00:15:28,317 --> 00:15:32,221
So "Asakusa Number One" was the name of a horse?

246
00:15:32,454 --> 00:15:34,056
Tch, get your words straight.

247
00:15:46,068 --> 00:15:49,805
Ryo-chan, you should say something. You haven't seen him in so long.

248
00:15:50,005 --> 00:15:54,543
Um, uh... Is your wife still making tsukudani?

249
00:15:55,244 --> 00:15:58,147
Yeah, I guess, by the by...

250
00:16:00,482 --> 00:16:02,818
Maybe you could lead the conversation?

251
00:16:03,018 --> 00:16:04,787
Ryotsu can be a bit shy.

252
00:16:04,987 --> 00:16:06,088
That so?

253
00:16:06,322 --> 00:16:12,628
Well, um... I've seen the cops in the media a lot these days.

254
00:16:12,828 --> 00:16:15,497
Must be hard for you guys on the beat.

255
00:16:15,698 --> 00:16:16,799
Not really.

256
00:16:17,266 --> 00:16:20,536
We're all pretty resigned on that...

257
00:16:20,736 --> 00:16:23,005
This is like watching a blind date.

258
00:16:23,205 --> 00:16:25,507
Anyone would think they're not even related.

259
00:16:42,091 --> 00:16:43,826
I can't stand this anymore!

260
00:16:45,594 --> 00:16:50,899
Ugh, and it's all my old man's fault for skipping work to bet on the horses.

261
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:54,370
If you're nursing an injury, you ought to be back home in bed.

262
00:16:54,703 --> 00:16:58,474
The hell? Who says a hernia should stop a man from betting on the races?

263
00:16:59,308 --> 00:17:00,743
Don't be so brash!

264
00:17:00,943 --> 00:17:04,847
If you'd stayed home like you should, we wouldn't have crossed paths here!

265
00:17:05,147 --> 00:17:08,684
It's your fault for daring to come to Asakusa in the first place!

266
00:17:08,884 --> 00:17:11,787
You said you'd never come back and then you ran off!

267
00:17:12,021 --> 00:17:15,791
We're only here because of stupid Reiko! It was nothing to do with me!

268
00:17:18,761 --> 00:17:19,928
Okay, calm down.

269
00:17:20,129 --> 00:17:23,899
We can't be bothering other patrons here. Let's go somewhere else.

270
00:17:24,099 --> 00:17:26,101
Excuse me! The check, please!

271
00:17:26,301 --> 00:17:27,636
Okay.

272
00:17:29,772 --> 00:17:30,706
Oh dear.

273
00:17:31,807 --> 00:17:35,244
What an unbelievable duo. I can't keep up with them at all.

274
00:17:35,444 --> 00:17:37,946
"DARUMAYA REST SPOT"

275
00:17:40,949 --> 00:17:43,185
Hey, this marble is blocking my drink.

276
00:17:43,419 --> 00:17:44,353
Come here, you...

277
00:17:46,522 --> 00:17:49,892
You gotta rest the marble against these bumps to drink.

278
00:17:50,092 --> 00:17:51,427
Oh, really?

279
00:17:52,261 --> 00:17:54,263
Well, that's how it is.

280
00:17:54,463 --> 00:17:56,265
He's as stubborn as they come.

281
00:17:56,465 --> 00:18:00,369
Now that I think about it, I guess I was being childish too.

282
00:18:00,836 --> 00:18:03,505
It's your fault for pushing tsukudani on me.

283
00:18:03,739 --> 00:18:06,909
They used to call me the "Tsukudani Kid" in school.

284
00:18:07,109 --> 00:18:10,946
We were trying to feed you so you'd grow up to be big and strong.

285
00:18:11,146 --> 00:18:14,016
Tsukudani all day every day only gets you malnourished.

286
00:18:14,216 --> 00:18:16,185
That logic's as silly as your face.

287
00:18:16,485 --> 00:18:20,189
You're criticizing my face? The apple never falls far from the tree.

288
00:18:20,389 --> 00:18:23,358
What was that? You stupid old fart!

289
00:18:23,759 --> 00:18:26,228
How dare you say that to your own father!

290
00:18:26,462 --> 00:18:29,665
-You wanna fight? Damn it! -Sure!

291
00:18:34,536 --> 00:18:35,337
There's a fire!

292
00:18:35,804 --> 00:18:36,538
Huh?

293
00:18:37,106 --> 00:18:38,540
Fire!

294
00:18:39,141 --> 00:18:40,642
A fire! There's a fire!

295
00:18:41,110 --> 00:18:42,311
Get outta the way!

296
00:18:42,511 --> 00:18:44,213
Hey, wait up, Pops!

297
00:18:44,413 --> 00:18:47,249
Move! Fires are when Tokyoites shine!

298
00:18:47,483 --> 00:18:49,518
Get outta the damn way!

299
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:53,722
They really are a lot alike.

300
00:18:53,956 --> 00:18:54,990
Move, move!

301
00:18:55,190 --> 00:18:56,225
Excuse us!

302
00:18:56,725 --> 00:18:58,494
Ah!

303
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,001
No fire engines yet?

304
00:19:06,201 --> 00:19:09,505
You've got to help! Mrs. Ofude is still in her apartment!

305
00:19:10,372 --> 00:19:11,073
Where is it?

306
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,175
Second floor, at the far end.

307
00:19:14,009 --> 00:19:15,043
I see it.

308
00:19:15,244 --> 00:19:16,078
Help!

309
00:19:17,813 --> 00:19:21,984
Kankichi! I'll save Miss Funbags, and you go save the old lady!

310
00:19:22,184 --> 00:19:24,286
Why do I get the old lady?

311
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,587
Wait, Dad!

312
00:19:25,821 --> 00:19:27,289
Hey, why do I have to...

313
00:19:27,523 --> 00:19:28,757
Here I come, bazongas!

314
00:19:28,991 --> 00:19:30,058
Why do I have to...

315
00:19:30,259 --> 00:19:31,560
Gotta save the boobies!

316
00:19:32,428 --> 00:19:33,562
Ma'am! Are you okay?

317
00:19:35,731 --> 00:19:36,431
Are you okay?

318
00:19:38,033 --> 00:19:40,002
I twisted my ankle...

319
00:19:40,302 --> 00:19:41,170
Hop on.

320
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:42,438
Thank you!

321
00:19:44,373 --> 00:19:45,941
&lt;i&gt;Feels so good...&lt;/i&gt;

322
00:19:46,175 --> 00:19:49,711
Okay, are you ready? Here we go...

323
00:19:53,015 --> 00:19:54,783
Dad, what are you doing? Hurry up!

324
00:19:55,317 --> 00:19:58,287
My back's flared up again.

325
00:19:58,654 --> 00:20:00,088
At a time like this?

326
00:20:00,289 --> 00:20:02,090
Hey, miss. Grab my shoulder!

327
00:20:02,291 --> 00:20:03,625
Okay!

328
00:20:04,626 --> 00:20:07,296
Dad, I'll be right back to help you!

329
00:20:25,647 --> 00:20:27,216
-Take them. -Got it.

330
00:20:27,416 --> 00:20:28,750
-Ryo-chan! -Ryotsu!

331
00:20:29,518 --> 00:20:30,652
What the heck?

332
00:20:32,321 --> 00:20:33,989
Ryotsu! What are you doing?

333
00:20:34,223 --> 00:20:35,891
I don't have time to explain!

334
00:20:36,091 --> 00:20:37,526
No, It's too dangerous.

335
00:20:37,759 --> 00:20:38,927
Leave it to us.

336
00:20:39,127 --> 00:20:40,762
Shut up! Move!

337
00:20:40,963 --> 00:20:42,130
I said no!

338
00:20:42,331 --> 00:20:44,433
Let go! My dad's still in there!

339
00:20:47,069 --> 00:20:48,170
-Ryotsu! -Ryo-chan!

340
00:20:53,242 --> 00:20:55,444
Damn it... What is Kankichi doing?

341
00:21:03,852 --> 00:21:04,720
Damn it...

342
00:21:04,953 --> 00:21:08,824
I should have asked him to make those bets for me.

343
00:21:12,361 --> 00:21:16,131
Don't be silly. This is no time for horse racing, you old fool!

344
00:21:16,565 --> 00:21:17,366
Kankichi!

345
00:21:29,478 --> 00:21:30,646
Ryo-chan!

346
00:21:30,846 --> 00:21:31,747
Ryotsu!

347
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:33,982
Oh no...

348
00:21:44,726 --> 00:21:45,560
Ryotsu!

349
00:21:45,761 --> 00:21:47,296
You had me so worried!

350
00:21:47,763 --> 00:21:50,766
It'll take more than this to kill me.

351
00:21:54,369 --> 00:21:56,405
"SANKICHI'S PLACE"

352
00:21:58,073 --> 00:22:01,376
Ouch... Reiko-chan, you need to be more gentle with me.

353
00:22:01,710 --> 00:22:02,577
I'm sorry.

354
00:22:03,045 --> 00:22:05,213
No need to apologize, Reiko.

355
00:22:05,414 --> 00:22:08,617
It's his own fault for acting like a pervert.

356
00:22:09,751 --> 00:22:11,620
Takes one to know one.

357
00:22:11,853 --> 00:22:12,721
What was that?

358
00:22:12,921 --> 00:22:17,392
Did you know that Kankichi used the women's bath right up until third grade?

359
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:21,229
That's enough! Who do you think saved your life?

360
00:22:21,797 --> 00:22:23,332
Who asked you to save me?

361
00:22:23,532 --> 00:22:26,802
I could have made it out on my own, but you had to interfere.

362
00:22:27,035 --> 00:22:28,904
You're just a useless old fossil!

363
00:22:29,237 --> 00:22:30,939
Say that again, you layabout!

364
00:22:34,276 --> 00:22:38,246
I know you're just getting started, but we need to leave before the chief...

365
00:22:38,714 --> 00:22:41,617
True, we did just slip out.

366
00:22:42,017 --> 00:22:43,752
Sorry, Pops. Take care.

367
00:22:46,288 --> 00:22:49,791
Thank you for the meal. I had a great time.

368
00:22:50,225 --> 00:22:51,493
I'm glad to hear it.

369
00:22:52,294 --> 00:22:53,395
We'll be off then.

370
00:22:54,396 --> 00:22:55,497
Kankichi...

371
00:22:56,198 --> 00:22:59,801
Won't you drop by sometime? Your mom's worried about you.

372
00:23:01,603 --> 00:23:02,738
Not today.

373
00:23:02,938 --> 00:23:05,307
This officer's got work to do.

374
00:23:05,774 --> 00:23:08,276
Head Patrol Officer Ryotsu, reporting for duty!

375
00:23:10,679 --> 00:23:11,913
Come again, Ryo-san.

376
00:23:12,214 --> 00:23:13,048
Yeah!

377
00:23:13,248 --> 00:23:13,982
See you.

378
00:23:18,387 --> 00:23:21,423
I reckon he's a Mommy's boy at heart.

379
00:23:22,791 --> 00:23:27,095
Still only a head patrol officer? At his age? What a loser.

380
00:23:27,863 --> 00:23:30,799
That's not true. He's become a fine policeman.

381
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:34,002
He'll always be a little boy to me.

382
00:23:34,236 --> 00:23:35,971
San-chan, another one, please?

383
00:23:36,438 --> 00:23:37,239
Sure thing!

384
00:23:37,806 --> 00:23:39,541
That moron.

385
00:23:43,645 --> 00:23:45,881
Your father is a lot of fun, Ryo-chan.

386
00:23:46,114 --> 00:23:46,815
Yeah.

387
00:23:47,349 --> 00:23:48,817
You two are very alike.

388
00:23:49,317 --> 00:23:50,819
Let's visit again, Ryotsu.

389
00:23:53,321 --> 00:23:54,823
Maybe once a year.

390
00:23:57,492 --> 00:23:59,027
See you again!

391
00:24:03,098 --> 00:24:08,904
HOUSE ARREST DOESN'T SCARE ME
